CHECKENV              BASIC UTILITY COMMAND           CHECKENV,CE 1Check environment variablesSYNTAX:  CHECKENV <eparam> <evalue>FUNCTION: This program allows the user to check the environment list, to check if a given variable has a particular setting.  The most common use would be in a .login file to set up the correct TERM variable.OPTIONS: NoneEXAMPLES: -nx          checkenv PORT /term ; setenv TERM st          checkenv PORT /t1   ; setenv TERM dr          -xNOTE: The above example will report an error message on the console for SEE ALSO: SETENV, UNSETENV, and PRINTENV utility command descriptions and the discussion of the SHELL environment in Chapter 5.COPYRIGHT:This program is copyright (1988) by Cowen Software Ltdof 21/23 Bristol Ave, Manchester, England, GB-M19 3NUIt is made available for any OS9/68K user freely,but may not be sold for profit, other than a reasonable handling charge